                <head>273. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On May 13 Herman Phleger delivered an address before the American Branch of the
                    International Law Association in New York City entitled “Recent Developments
                    Affecting the Regime of the High Seas.” Among the matters discussed by Phleger
                    were freedom of the seas, conservation of fishery resources, and the Continental
                    Shelf. The text of the address is printed in Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, June 6, 1955, pages 934-940.</p>
            </div>
